abstract: >-
  sel2pw is an open-source Node.js package that performs deterministic,
  rule-based migration of legacy Selenium test suites to Playwright TypeScript
  scaffolds intended for human completion. The Java frontend (TestNG/JUnit/Cucumber)
  extracts from a java-parser AST and falls back to a regex extractor when AST
  parsing fails; the C# frontend (NUnit/SpecFlow) is a regex/balanced-brace
  extractor and is experimental. Every construct the rule catalogue does not cover
  is emitted as an explicit stub with a migration recipe rather than silently
  dropped; an optional, off-by-default LLM fallback can propose translations for
  such constructs. On a benchmark of 15 open-source Selenium repositories (409 Java
  source files, LLM fallback disabled) every file produced an output or an explicit
  skip record (no crashes): 150 files were converted with no stubs, 152 contained
  stubs, 96 needed mixed cleanup and 11 were skipped as data-only classes. Output
  generally requires manual completion before it compiles; per-file TypeScript
  error counts are reported in CONVERSION_REVIEW.md (line-level punch list) and
  MIGRATION_NOTES.md (project-wide guidance).
